@startuml
'==== Title ====
title "As a Buyer, I want to use the Web UI to bid on an auction." - SD

'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

' ==== Actor and participants ====
actor User
participant ":WebUI" as CLI
participant ":AuctionRestController" as Controller

User -> CLI : I would like to know %n() what I can do in %n() regard to an existing %n()auction
activate CLI
CLI -> Controller : OPTIONS /auctions/{auctionId} { ... }
activate Controller

ref over Controller
[[rest-sd-ref-diagrams/OPTIONS_Place_Bid_SD.puml OPTIONS for user on /auctions/{auctionId}]]
end ref

Controller --> CLI : 200 OK + _links
deactivate Controller
CLI --> User : display HATEOAS %n() links
deactivate CLI

User -> CLI : I want to place a %n() bid on an auction
activate CLI
CLI -> Controller : POST /auctions/{auctionId}/bids %n(){ DTORequest } + userIdFromHeader
activate Controller

ref over Controller
[[rest-sd-ref-diagrams/POST_Place_Bid_SD.puml POST (place bid on auction)]]
end ref

Controller --> CLI : 201 Created + BidResponseDTO
deactivate Controller
CLI --> User : Bid successfully %n() placed.
deactivate CLI

@enduml